"""
## Purpose and audience

This specification is maintained for compiler and library engineers reviewing FIXTURES-BINPROV behavior, and for operators verifying a build.

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test --no-session-daemon test/fixtures/binprov/binary_provenance_probe_spec.spl` and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario names the requirement it traces to and starts with a Verify step.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the behavior explicitly asserted below on the current toolchain. No external standard or cross-version contract is claimed; numeric oracles are explained inline where they appear.

## Recovery and troubleshooting

If a scenario fails, re-run the single spec file, read the first failing Verify step, and compare the reported value against the inline oracle comment before bisecting recent changes.
"""
use std.spec.{step}
# @manual: primary
# REQ-FIXTURES-BINPROV-001
# doc-path: doc/01_research/app/
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/app/
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/app/
# doc-path: doc/05_design/app/
# Probe spec for the child-binary provenance trap. Trivial on purpose: it must
# reveal WHICH binary ran (via the runner's `child binary:` line), never
# pass/fail-reveal — a pass/fail probe reintroduces the ambiguity the defect
# exploits. See doc/08_tracking/bug/
# simple_test_child_binary_ignores_invoking_binary_recurrence_2026-08-08.md.
fn main():
    describe("binary provenance probe"):
        it("runs"):
            # @req: REQ-FIXTURES-BINPROV-001
            step("Verify: runs")
            # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
            assert_true(true)
